{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Corrupt_Heart","to":"Corrupt Heart"},{"from":"Time_Eater","to":"Time Eater"},{"from":"Snake_Plant","to":"Snake Plant"},{"from":"Donu_and_Deca","to":"Donu and Deca"},{"from":"Centurion_and_Mystic","to":"Centurion and Mystic"},{"from":"Spire_Shield_and_Spire_Spear","to":"Spire Shield and Spire Spear"},{"from":"Spheric_Guardian","to":"Spheric Guardian"},{"from":"The_Guardian","to":"The Guardian"},{"from":"Writhing_Mass","to":"Writhing Mass"},{"from":"Book_of_Stabbing","to":"Book of Stabbing"}],"pages":{"2579":{"pageid":2579,"ns":0,"title":"Book of Stabbing","revisions":[{"revid":53474,"parentid":53473,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Book of Stabbing\n|Image  = BookOfStabbing.png\n|HP     = 160-164\n|AscHP  = 168-172\n|Powers = {{BD|Painful Stabs}}\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Elite\n}} {{Power Infobox|Painful Stabs}}\nBook of Stabbing is an [[Elite]] enemy found exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Book of Stabbing}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Multi Stab\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (6\u00d7N;{{Asc|3|7\u00d7N}}) damage. (N = Number of times {{Int|Book of Stabbing|Multi Stab}} was used this combat, plus 2.; On {{Asc|18|}}, N = Current turn, plus 1.)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Big Stab\n|Intent = Attack5\n|Effect = Deals (21;{{Asc|3|24}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n15% chance to use {{Int|Book of Stabbing|Big Stab}} and an 85% chance to use {{Int|Book of Stabbing|Multi Stab}}.\n\nCannot use {{Int|Book of Stabbing|Multi Stab}} 3 times in a row and cannot use {{Int|Book of Stabbing|Big Stab}} twice in a row.\n\n== Found With ==\n\n=== Act 2 ===\n* Solo\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Book of Stabbing appears in the artwork of {{C|Safety}}.\n* While this enemy does not return in the sequel, the {{BD|Painful Stabs}} effect is reused for the Act 3 boss {{M2|Test Subject}}'s second phase.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"2471":{"pageid":2471,"ns":0,"title":"Centurion and Mystic","revisions":[{"revid":56931,"parentid":55685,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"= Centurion =\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Centurion\n|Image  = Centurion.png\n|HP     = 76-80\n|AscHP  = 78-83\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Centurion''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Centurion}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Slash\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (12;{{Asc|2|14}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Protect\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = {{M|Mystic}} gains (15;{{Asc|17|20}}) {{KW|Block}}. If alone, instead gains (15;{{Asc|17|20}}) {{KW|Block}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Block\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Fury\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (6\u00d73;{{Asc|2|7\u00d73}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Centurion''' will use one of the following actions each turn if the {{M|Mystic}} is alive:\n* {{Int|Centurion|Slash}} (65% chance)\n* {{Int|Centurion|Protect}} (35% chance)\nIf the {{M|Mystic}} is dead, '''Centurion''' will replace {{Int|Centurion|Protect}} with {{Int|Centurion|Fury}}. '''Centurion''' will never use any move three times in a row.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside:\n* 1 {{M|Mystic}}\n\n= Mystic =\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Mystic\n|Image  = Healer.png\n|HP     = 48-56\n|AscHP  = 50-58\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Mystic''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Mystic}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Attack\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (8;{{Asc|2|9}}) damage. Applies 2 {{BD|Frail}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Frail\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Buff\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = All enemies gain (2;{{Asc|2|3}} ; {{Asc|17|4}}) {{BD|Strength}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Strength\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Heal\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = All enemies heal (16;{{Asc|17|20}}) HP.\n|GivesToEnemy = Heal\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nIf an enemy is missing 16 ({{Asc|19|21}}) or more HP, '''Mystic''' will use {{Int|Mystic|Heal}}, up to twice in a row. Otherwise, '''Mystic''' will use one of the following actions each turn:\n* {{Int|Mystic|Attack}} (60% chance)\n* {{Int|Mystic|Buff}} (40% chance)\nMystic will never use {{Int|Mystic|Attack}} or {{Int|Mystic|Buff}} three times in a row.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, '''Mystic''' will never use {{Int|Mystic|Attack}} twice in a row.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside:\n* 1 {{M|Centurion}}\n<!--\n= Tips =\n\n= Trivia =\n-->\n= Update History =\n* Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!\n** Centurion's animation is now a bit less 3D and slowed by 20%.\n\n* Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!\n** Centurion gets new animations.\n** The Mystic gets new animations.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2384":{"pageid":2384,"ns":0,"title":"Chosen","revisions":[{"revid":56936,"parentid":55693,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Ambox\n| title = WARNING!\n| color = red\n| icon = GremlinNob.png\n| message = ''This page is under construction. Information may be wrong or incomplete.''\n}}\n\n\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Chosen\n|Image  = Chosen.png\n|HP     = 95-99\n|AscHP  = 98-103\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Hex}}'''The Chosen''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] encountered exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Chosen}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Poke\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (5\u00d72;{{Asc|2|6\u00d72}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Hex\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies {{BD|Hex}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Hex\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Debilitate\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage. Applies 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Drain\n|Intent = DebuffDefend\n|Effect = Applies 3 {{BD|Weak}}. Gain 3 {{BD|Strength}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Strength\n|GivesToPlayer = Weak\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Zap\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (18;{{Asc|2|21}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlways starts with {{Int|Chosen|Poke}} followed by {{Int|Chosen|Hex}}. After that, repeats the following pattern for the rest of the combat:\n#{{Int|Chosen|Debilitate}} (50% chance) or {{Int|Chosen|Drain}} (50% chance)\n#{{Int|Chosen|Poke}} (60% chance) or {{Int|Chosen|Zap}} (40% chance)\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, '''Chosen''' always starts with {{Int|Chosen|Hex}} instead of {{Int|Chosen|Poke}}.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs an easy pool encounter:\n* Solo\n\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside either:\n* 1 {{M|Byrd}}\n* 1 {{M|Cultist}}\n<!--\n== Tips ==\n* You can block Hex with Artifact.\n-->\n== Lore ==\n'''Chosen''' are implied to be connected to the {{M|Cultist|Cultists}} and {{M|Awakened One}} in some way, as they all share a blue crow motif.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The '''Chosen''' is the only thing in the game that can apply {{BD|Hex}}.\n* '''Chosen''' appears in the artwork of {{C|Immolate}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader\n** The Chosen enemy's AI is now less random.\n\n* Weekly Patch 19: Seed\n** Fixed the turn order for Chosen + Byrd encounter. Chosen no longer applies Vulnerable before Byrd attacks.\n\n* Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life\n** Adding Cultist + Chosen encounter into City.\n\n* Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things\n** Hex Power wording improvements.\n\n* Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!\n** The Chosen gets new animations.\n\n* Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance\n** Chosen enemy buffed.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"3030":{"pageid":3030,"ns":0,"title":"Corrupt Heart","revisions":[{"revid":56949,"parentid":56636,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Corrupt Heart\n|Image  = CorruptHeart.png\n|Icon   = Map-CorruptHeart.png\n|HP     = 750\n|AscHP  = 800\n|Powers = {{BD|Beat of Death}} 1 ({{Asc|19|2}}) <br> {{BD|Invincible}} 300 ({{Asc|19|200}})\n|Debut  = Act 4\n|Type   = Boss\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name=Beat of Death\n|Image=Icon_BeatOfDeath.png\n|Description=Whenever you play a card, take X damage.\n|Stacks=Intensity\n|Type=Buff\n|BetweenTurns=Permanent\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name=Invincible\n|Image=Icon_Invincible.png\n|Description=Can only lose X more HP this turn.\n|Stacks=Intensity\n|Type=Buff\n|BetweenTurns=Reset\n}}\nThe Corrupt Heart is the final boss, found at the end of [[Act 4]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Corrupt Heart}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Debilitate\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}, 2 {{BD|Weak}} and 2 {{BD|Frail}}. Adds 1 {{C|Burn}}, 1 {{C|Dazed}}, 1 {{C|Slimed}}, 1 {{C|Void}} and 1 {{C|Wound}} into your draw pile.\n|GivesToPlayer = Vulnerable, Weak, Frail\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Blood Shots\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (2\u00d712;{{Asc|4|2\u00d715}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Echo\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (40;{{Asc|4|45}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Buff\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Loses all negative {{BD|Strength}}, then gains 2 {{BD|Strength}}. Gains an additional [[Buffs|Buff]]:\n* 1st buff: 2 {{BD|Artifact}}\n* 2nd buff: 1 {{BD|Beat of Death}}\n* 3rd buff: {{BD|Painful Stabs}}\n* 4th buff: 10 {{BD|Strength}}\n* 5th buff: 50 {{BD|Strength}}\n|GivesToEnemy = Strength, Artifact, Beat of Death, Painful Stabs\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlways starts with {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Debilitate}}. Uses {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Buff}} every 3 turns starting from turn 4.\n\nOn all other turns it has a 50/50 chance to use either {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Blood Shots}} followed by {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Echo}} or {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Echo}} followed by {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Blood Shots}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{C|Mental Fortress}} activates before {{BD|Beat of Death}} for every {{KW|Stance}} changing card, except for {{C|Indignation}} which activates after.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]},"1469":{"pageid":1469,"ns":0,"title":"Cultist","revisions":[{"revid":56342,"parentid":55715,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n| Name   = Cultist\n| Image  = Cultist.png\n| HP     = 48-54\n| AscHP  = 50-56\n| Debut  = Act 1\n| Type   = Normal\n}}'''The Cultist''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that can show up in all 3 Acts.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Cultist}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Incantation\n| Intent = Buff\n| Effect = Gains (3;{{Asc|2|4}} ; {{Asc|17|5}}) {{BD|Ritual}}.\n| GivesToEnemy = Ritual\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Dark Strike\n| Intent = Attack2\n| Effect = Deals 6 damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nAlways starts with {{Int|Cultist|Incantation}}, then uses {{Int|Cultist|Dark Strike}} every turn after.\n\n== In Party With ==\n\n=== Act 1 ===\nAs an easy pool encounter:\n\n* Solo\n\nAs half of an Exordium Thugs encounter in the hard pool:\n\n* 1 {{M|Acid Slime (M)}}\n* 1 {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}\n* 1 {{M|Green Louse}}\n* 1 {{M|Red Louse}}\n\n=== Act 2 ===\nIn the hard pool alongside:\n\n* 2 other Cultists\n* 1 {{M|Chosen}}\n\n=== Act 3 ===\nIn the {{M|Awakened One}} boss fight, alongside:\n* 1 other Cultist\n\n== Lore ==\nThey are strongly implied to worship the crow god Mazaleth, and implied to have a connection to the {{M|Chosen}} and {{M|Awakened One}}. Their {{R|Cultist Headpiece|Headpiece}} can be acquired in the {{E|Face Trader}} event. The {{P|Cultist Potion}}, which grants the player 1 {{BD|Ritual}}, is a reference to this enemy.\n\n\nAt the Act 2 [[Event]] {{E|The Nest}}, a bit of their mode of operation can be gleaned.\n\n<blockquote>\nA long line of <span class=\"defect-text\">hooded figures</span> can be seen entering an \n<span class=\"watcher-text\">unassuming cathedral</span>.\n\nNaturally, you join the line and are quickly surrounded by <span class=\"ironclad-text\">Cultists!</span>\n\nThey ignore you as they gleefully chant and wave their weapons around.\n\nCultists: <span class=\"ironclad-text\">\"MURDER!! MURDER MURDER!!\"</span>\n\nCultists: <span class=\"defect-text\">\"CAW CAW CAAAAAWWW!\"</span>\n\nCultists: <span class=\"ironclad-text\">\"MURDER! MURDER MUURDER!!\"</span>\n\nCultists: <span class=\"defect-text\">\"CAAW CAW CAAAAAAWW!!\"</span>\n\nYou eye a <span class=\"rare-font\">Donation Box... </span>\n</blockquote>\n\n<blockquote>\nYou decide to stay in line (out of fear) to see what will happen.\n\nEventually, you are face-to-face with the leader. A well-dressed cultist hands you an \n<span class=\"rare-font\">Ornate Dagger.</span> Like the others before you, you slash your forearm and let the blood drip into a misshapen bowl.\n\nThe cultists chant and holler for you!\n\nCultists: <span class=\"defect-text\">\"CAAW CAW CAAAAAAWW!!\"</span>\n\nYou chant, too. Why not?\n</blockquote>\n\n* The most comprehensive lore regarding Cultists was put together by TiberiusEsuriens <ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/slaythespire/comments/lwc6tu/connecting_lore_birds/</ref>\n\n\n== Trivia ==\n* They are the only enemy that can appear in every standard Act (Act 1, Act 2, and Act 3).\n\n* Cultists appear in the artwork of {{C|Immolate}}, {{C|Sash Whip}}, {{C|Vault}} and {{C|Swift Strike}}. They are also found in the [[Beta Art]] of several cards including {{C|Prostrate}}, {{C|Disarm}}, and {{C|Choke}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"3029":{"pageid":3029,"ns":0,"title":"Donu and Deca","revisions":[{"revid":55733,"parentid":51690,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"Donu and Deca is a [[Bosses|Boss Encounter]] found at the end of [[Act 3]].\n\n== Donu ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Donu\n|Image  = Donu.png\n|Icon   = Map-DonuDeca.png\n|HP     = 250\n|AscHP  = 265\n|Powers = {{BD|Artifact}} 2 ({{Asc|19|3}})\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Boss\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Artifact}}\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Donu}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Circle of Power\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = All enemies gain 3 {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Beam\n|Intent = Attack6\n|Effect = Deals (10\u00d72;{{Asc|4|12\u00d72}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlternates between {{Int|Donu|Circle of Power}} and {{Int|Donu|Beam}}.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Deca ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Deca\n|Image  = Deca.png\n|Icon   = Map-DonuDeca.png\n|HP     = 250\n|AscHP  = 265\n|Powers = {{BD|Artifact}} 2 ({{Asc|19|3}})\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Boss\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Artifact}}\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Deca}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Beam\n|Intent = DebuffAttack5\n|Effect = Deals (10\u00d72;{{Asc|4|12\u00d72}}) damage. Adds 2 {{C|Dazed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Square of Protection\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = All enemies gain 16 {{KW|Block}}(; and {{Asc|19|3}} {{BD|Plated Armor}}).}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nAlternates between {{Int|Deca|Beam}} and {{Int|Deca|Square of Protection}}.\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Achievements ==\n* '''The Shapes''': Defeat Donu and Deca.\n* '''Ooh Donut!''': Finish Donu with a {{C|Feed}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Donu appears in the artwork of {{C|Bullseye}}.\n* Despite Deca's name being the Greek root for 10, Deca is an octahedron.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]},"2515":{"pageid":2515,"ns":0,"title":"Gremlins","revisions":[{"revid":56126,"parentid":55772,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"'''Gremlins''' are encountered as normal [[Monsters|Enemies]] in [[Act 1]]. In [[Act 2]], Gremlins appear only as {{BD|Minion|Minions}} in the {{M|Gremlin Leader|Gremlin Leader's}} [[Elite]] encounter.\n{{TOC limit|2}}\n\n== Fat Gremlin ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Fat Gremlin\n|Image  = GremlinFat.png\n|HP     = 13-17\n|AscHP  = 14-18\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Fat Gremlins''' focus on applying {{BD|Weak}}.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Fat Gremlin}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Smash\n|Intent = DebuffAttack1\n|Effect = Deals (4;{{Asc|2|5}}) damage. Applies 1 {{BD|Weak}}(.; and {{Asc|17|1}} {{BD|Frail}}.)}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Fat Gremlin''' uses {{Int|Fat Gremlin|Smash}} every turn.\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Mad Gremlin ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Mad Gremlin\n|Image  = MadGremlin.png\n|HP     = 20-24\n|AscHP  = 21-25\n|Powers = {{BD|Angry}} 1 ({{Asc|17|2}})\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}} {{Power Infobox|Angry}}\n'''Mad Gremlins''' will do more damage as they are attacked.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Mad Gremlin}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Scratch\n|Intent = Attack1\n|Effect = Deals (4;{{Asc|2|5}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Mad Gremlin''' uses {{Int|Mad Gremlin|Scratch}} every turn.\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Shield Gremlin ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Shield Gremlin\n|Image  = GremlinTsundere.png\n|HP     = 12-15\n|AscHP  = 13-17\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Shield Gremlins''' focus on giving {{KW|Block}} to their allies.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Shield Gremlin}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Protect\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = Random enemy gains (7;{{Asc|2|8}} ; {{Asc|17|11}}) {{KW|Block}}. Only chooses self if alone.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Shield Bash\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (6;{{Asc|2|8}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Shield Gremlin''' uses {{Int|Shield Gremlin|Protect}} every turn. If it is the only enemy left, it will switch to using {{Int|Shield Gremlin|Shield Bash}} every turn.\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Sneaky Gremlin ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Sneaky Gremlin\n|Image  = GremlinThief.png\n|HP     = 10-14\n|AscHP  = 11-15\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Sneaky Gremlins''' focus on doing consistent damage each turn.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Sneaky Gremlin}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Puncture\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (9;{{Asc|2|10}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Sneaky Gremlin''' uses {{Int|Sneaky Gremlin|Puncture}} every turn.\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Gremlin Wizard ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Gremlin Wizard\n|Image  = GremlinWizard.png\n|HP     = 21-25\n|AscHP  = 22-26\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Gremlin Wizards''' charge up before unleashing a powerful attack.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Gremlin Wizard}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Charging\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Does nothing.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Ultimate Blast\n|Intent = Attack6\n|Effect = Deals (25;{{Asc|2|30}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Gremlin Wizard''' will always start by using {{Int|Gremlin Wizard|Charging}} twice in a row, then using {{Int|Gremlin Wizard|Ultimate Blast}}. After that and for the rest of combat, '''Gremlin Wizard''' will use {{Int|Gremlin Wizard|Charging}} three times in a row before using {{Int|Gremlin Wizard|Ultimate Blast}}.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, '''Gremlin Wizard''' will use {{Int|Gremlin Wizard|Charging}} twice in a row, then use {{Int|Gremlin Wizard|Ultimate Blast}} every turn for the rest of combat.\n{{Clear}}\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 1 ===\nIn the '''Gremlin Gang''' encounter, randomly choosing from the following list for a total of 4 enemies:\n* 2 {{M|Fat Gremlin|Fat Gremlins}}\n* 2 {{M|Sneaky Gremlin|Sneaky Gremlins}}\n* 2 {{M|Mad Gremlin|Mad Gremlins}}\n* 1 {{M|Shield Gremlin}}\n* 1 {{M|Gremlin Wizard}}\n\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs {{BD|Minion|Minions}} in an Elite encounter consisting of:\n* 2 random '''Gremlins'''\n* 1 {{M|Gremlin Leader}}\n\n= Tips =\n* Gremlins summoned by {{M|Gremlin Leader}} will always have the {{BD|Minion}} [[Buff]], so the effects of {{KW|Fatal}} will not work on them.\n\n= Trivia =\n* The {{E|Wheel of Change}} and {{E|Match and Keep}} [[Events]] are run by Gremlins.\n* {{R|Gremlin Visage}} is a reference to Gremlins, although it doesn't resemble any of the types seen in the game.\n** {{R|Gremlin Horn}} also references Gremlins, specifically {{M|Gremlin Nob}}.\n* Mad Gremlin appears in the artwork of {{C|Riddle with Holes}} and {{C|Trip}}.\n* An unidentified Gremlin appears in the artwork of {{C|Cleave}}, {{C|Hemokinesis}}, {{C|Reckless Charge}}, {{C|Sever Soul}}, {{C|Eviscerate}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Rip and Tear}}, {{C|Bowling Bash}} and {{C|Expunger}}.\n\n= Update History =\n* Patch V1.1: The Dealer\n** Fixed enemy order issues in Slime Boss, Gremlin Leader, and Reptomancer encounters.\n\n* Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!\n** Asc 17 Gremlin Wizard no longer attacks a turn early, but now keeps attacking.\n\n* Weekly Patch 33: Terror\n** Gremlin Leader summon used the incorrect RNG, resulting in different enemies for the same seed.\n\n* Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning\n** Gremlin Leader's minion summon is now seeded.\n\n* Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face\n** Fixed issue where Shield Gremlin and Orb Walker had upped values in the wrong Ascension Level.\n\n* Weekly Patch 15: Surprise Patch\n** Fixed issue where Gremlin Thief stopped using Ascension 2 damage after first hit.\n\n* Weekly Patch 14: Bullet Time\n** In Fast Mode, Gremlin Leader's minions spawn a lot faster.\n\n* Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!\n** Little gremlins no longer yell about escaping if they're dead. Corpses don't yell.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]\n[[Category:Minions]]"}}}]},"2578":{"pageid":2578,"ns":0,"title":"Lagavulin","revisions":[{"revid":55835,"parentid":53472,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Lagavulin\n|Image  = LagavulinAwake.png\n|HP     = 109-111\n|AscHP  = 112-115\n|Powers = {{BD|Metallicize}} 8 <br> {{KW|Block}} 8\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Elite\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Metallicize}}\nLagavulin is an [[Elite]] enemy found exclusively in [[Act 1]] or in the {{E|Dead Adventurer}} Event.\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Lagavulin}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Sleep\n|Intent = Sleep\n|Effect = Does nothing.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Stunned\n|Intent = Stunned\n|Effect = Does nothing.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Attack\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (18;{{Asc|3|20}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Siphon Soul\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies (-1;{{Asc|18|-2}}) {{BD|Dexterity}} and (-1;{{Asc|18|-2}}) {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n=== When found in an Elite encounter: ===\n[[File:Lagavulin.png|140px|left|thumb|Lagavulin asleep.]]\nStarts off {{Int|Lagavulin|Sleep|Sleeping}}. If it takes any damage, it will be stunned for one turn and then proceed to attack. If three turns pass without any damage taken, it will awake and immediately begin attacking. Once awoken, its {{BD|Metallicize}} will be removed.\n\nWhen attacking it will repeat this pattern:\n* {{Int|Lagavulin|Attack}}\n* {{Int|Lagavulin|Attack}}\n* {{Int|Lagavulin|Siphon Soul}}\n<br> <br> \n\n=== When found in the {{E|Dead Adventurer}} fight: ===\n\nSpawns already awake and will repeat this pattern:\n\n* {{Int|Lagavulin|Siphon Soul}}\n* {{Int|Lagavulin|Attack}}\n* {{Int|Lagavulin|Attack}}\n\n== Found With ==\n\n=== Act 1 ===\n* Solo\n* Can be found in the {{E|Dead Adventurer}} when choosing {{Frame|Search}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"2583":{"pageid":2583,"ns":0,"title":"Nemesis","revisions":[{"revid":53506,"parentid":53505,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Nemesis\n|Image  = Nemesis.png\n|HP     = 185\n|AscHP  = 200\n|Powers = {{BD|Intangible}} every other turn\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Elite\n}} {{Power Infobox|Intangible}}\nNemesis is an [[Elite]] enemy found exclusively in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Nemesis}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tri Attack\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (6\u00d73;{{Asc|3|7\u00d73}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tri Burn\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Adds (3;{{Asc|18|5}}) {{C|Burn|Burns}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Scythe\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals 45 damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nOn its first turn has a 50/50 chance of using either {{Int|Nemesis|Tri Burn}} or {{Int|Nemesis|Tri Attack}}.\n\nAfterwards it has ''approximately'' these chances:\n* {{Int|Nemesis|Tri Burn}} (35% chance)\n* {{Int|Nemesis|Tri Attack}} (35% chance)\n* {{Int|Nemesis|Scythe}} (30% chance)\n\nCannot use {{Int|Nemesis|Tri Burn}} or {{Int|Nemesis|Scythe}} twice in a row. Cannot use {{Int|Nemesis|Tri Attack}} three times in a row.\n\n== Found With ==\n\n=== Act 3 ===\n* Solo\n\n== Lore ==\n\nWhen completing the Act 3 event {{E|Sensory Stone}}, you 'recall' what appear to be memories regarding the pasts of the characters. The {{TS|green||TRIUMPH}} dialogue option may recall a battle between the [[Silent]] and the [[Nemesis]], and her reason for climbing the Spire.\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">{{TS|green|up|TRIUMPH}}<br>\n\nThe remains of a {{TS|purple|up|ghostly creature}} sink slowly into the mud before you, barely visible in the moonlight. You have proven yourself amongst your sisters.<br>\n\nStanding victoriously, you wait in silence as the others ceremoniously place the {{TS|gold||creature's skull}} atop your head. The ritual has concluded.<br>\n\nYou head towards the Spire...</div></blockquote>\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"2584":{"pageid":2584,"ns":0,"title":"Reptomancer","revisions":[{"revid":55719,"parentid":53509,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Reptomancer\n|Image  = Reptomancer.png\n|HP     = 180-190\n|AscHP  = 190-200\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Elite\n}}\nReptomancer is an [[Elite]] enemy found exclusively in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Reptomancer}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Spawn Dagger\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Summons (1 {{M|Dagger}};{{Asc|18|2}} {{M|Dagger|Daggers}}) (up to a maximum of 4).}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Big Bite\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (30;{{Asc|3|34}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Snake Strike\n|Intent = DebuffAttack6\n|Effect = Deals (13\u00d72;{{Asc|3|16\u00d72}}) damage. Applies 1 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nAlways starts with {{Int|Reptomancer|Spawn Dagger}}.\n\nAfterward it has an approximately equal chance of using {{Int|Reptomancer|Snake Strike}}, {{Int|Reptomancer|Big Bite}}, and {{Int|Reptomancer|Spawn Dagger}}.\n\nCannot use {{Int|Reptomancer|Snake Strike}} or {{Int|Reptomancer|Big Bite}} twice in a row. Cannot use {{Int|Reptomancer|Spawn Dagger}} three times in a row.\n\nOnly 4 {{M|Dagger|Daggers}} can be in play at any time. If {{Int|Reptomancer|Spawn Dagger}} was chosen with 4 {{M|Dagger|Daggers}} in play, it will use {{Int|Reptomancer|Snake Strike}} instead.\n\n== Found With ==\n=== Act 3 ===\n* Two other {{M|Dagger|Daggers}}\n\n= Dagger =\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Dagger\n|Image  = Dagger.png\n|HP     = 20-25\n|AscHP  = 20-25\n|Powers = {{BD|Minion}}\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Minion\n}}\nDagger is a {{BD|Minion}} enemy summoned only by Reptomancer.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Dagger}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Wound\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals 9 damage. Adds a {{C|Wound}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Explode\n|Intent = Attack6\n|Effect = Deals 25 damage. Dies}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nUses {{Int|Dagger|Wound}} and then {{Int|Dagger|Explode}}.\n\n== Found With ==\nSummoned during the Reptomancer fight and also found at the start of combat with:\n* One other Dagger\n* Reptomancer\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Minions]]\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"2249":{"pageid":2249,"ns":0,"title":"Slimes","revisions":[{"revid":55614,"parentid":53423,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{TOC limit|2}}\n== Spike Slime (L) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spike Slime (L)\n|Image  = SpikeSlimeL.png\n|HP     = 64-70\n|AscHP  = 67-73\n|Powers = {{BD|Split}}\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Split}}\n'''Spike Slime (L)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spike Slime (L)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies (2;{{Asc|17|3}}) {{BD|Frail}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Flame Tackle\n|Intent = DebuffAttack4\n|Effect = Deals (16;{{Asc|2|18}}) damage. Adds 2 {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Split\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Disappears and spawns 2 {{M|Spike Slime (M)|Spike Slimes (M)}} with its current HP.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nHas a 30% chance of using {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Flame Tackle}} and a 70% chance of using {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Lick}}. Cannot use the same move three times in a row.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, it cannot use {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Lick}} twice in a row.\n\nOnce its HP reaches 50% or lower, its current [[Intent]] will be interrupted and changed to {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Split}}.\n\n=== Found With ===\nIt is only found by itself in combat.\n\n== Spike Slime (M) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spike Slime (M)\n|Image  = SpikeSlimeM.png\n|HP     = 28-32\n|AscHP  = 29-34\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Spike Slime (M)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spike Slime (M)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 1 {{BD|Frail}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Flame Tackle\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (8;{{Asc|2|10}}) damage. Adds a {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nIdentical to {{M|Spike Slime (L)}} but it cannot {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Split}}.\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nCan be in the Easy Pool's '''Small Slimes''' encounter with an {{M|Acid Slime (S)}}.\n\nCan be a part of the '''Exordium Thugs''' encounter along with either:\n\n* One of the [[Slavers]]\n* {{M|Cultist}}\n* {{M|Looter}}\n\nCan be a part of the '''Exordium Wildlife''' encounter along with either:\n\n* {{M|Fungi Beast}}\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n\n== Spike Slime (S) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spike Slime (S)\n|Image  = SpikeSlimeS.png\n|HP     = 10-14\n|AscHP  = 11-15\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Spike Slime (S)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that is exclusively found in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spike Slime (S)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (5;{{Asc|2|6}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nCan be in the Easy Pool's '''Small Slimes''' encounter with an {{M|Acid Slime (M)}}.\n\nIn the '''Lots of Slimes''' encounter with:\n\n* Two other {{M|Spike Slime (S)|Spike Slimes (S)}}\n* Two {{M|Acid Slime (S)|Small Acid Slimes}}\n\n== Acid Slime (L) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Acid Slime (L)\n|Image  = AcidSlimeL.png\n|HP     = 65-69\n|AscHP  = 68-72\n|Powers = {{BD|Split}}\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}{{Power Infobox|Split}}\n'''Acid Slime (L)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] exclusively found in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Acid Slime (L)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Corrosive Spit\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (11;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage. Adds 2 {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 2 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (16;{{Asc|2|18}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Split\n|Intent = Unknown\n|Effect = Disappears and spawns 2 {{M|Acid Slime (M)|Acid Slimes (M)}} with its current HP.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nHas a 30% ({{Asc|17|40%}}) chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Corrosive Spit}}, a 40% ({{Asc|17|30%}}) chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Tackle}} and a 30% chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Lick}} every turn.\n\nCannot use {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Tackle}} ({{Asc|17|Lick}}) twice in a row and cannot use other moves three times in a row.\n\nOnce its HP reaches 50% or lower, its current [[Intent]] will be interrupted and changed to {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Split}}.\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nOnly found solo.\n\n== Acid Slime (M) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Acid Slime (M)\n|Image  = AcidSlimeM.png\n|HP     = 28-32\n|AscHP  = 29-34\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Acid Slime (M)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Acid Slime (M)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Corrosive Spit\n|Intent = DebuffAttack2\n|Effect = Deals (7;{{Asc|2|8}}) damage. Adds a {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 1 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nIdentical pattern to {{M|Acid Slime (L)}} but it cannot {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Split}}.\n\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}: Every turn it has a 40% change of using {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Corrosive Spit}}, a 40% chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Tackle}}, and a 20% chance of using {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Lick}}. {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Lick}} cannot be used twice in a row and other moves cannot be used 3 times in a row.\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nCan be in the Easy Pool's '''Small Slimes''' encounter with a {{M|Spike Slime (S)}}.\n\nCan be a part of the '''Exordium Thugs''' encounter along with either:\n* One of the [[Slavers]]\n* {{M|Cultist}}\n* {{M|Looter}}\nCan be found as half of the '''Exordium Wildlife''' encounter with either:\n\n* {{M|Fungi Beast}}\n* {{M|Jaw Worm}}\n\n== Acid Slime (S) ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Acid Slime (S)\n|Image  = AcidSlimeS.png\n|HP     = 8-12\n|AscHP  = 9-13\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n'''Acid Slime (S)''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that is exclusively found in Act 1.\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Acid Slime (S)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lick\n|Intent = Debuff\n|Effect = Applies 1 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Tackle\n|Intent = Attack1\n|Effect = Deals (3;{{Asc|2|4}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n=== Found With ===\n\n===== Act 1 =====\nCan be in the Easy Pool's '''Small Slimes''' encounter with a {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}.\n\nIn the '''Lots of Slimes''' encounter with:\n\n* One other {{M|Acid Slime (S)}}\n* Three {{M|Spike Slime (S)|Small Spike Slimes}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Acid Slimes appear in the artwork of {{C|Evolve}}, {{C|Intimidate}}, {{C|Nightmare}}, {{C|Consecrate}}, {{C|Halt}} and {{C|Thinking Ahead}}.\n* Spike Slimes appear in the artwork of {{C|Carnage}}, {{C|Reaper}}, {{C|Grand Finale}} and {{C|Conclude}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"3049":{"pageid":3049,"ns":0,"title":"Snake Plant","revisions":[{"revid":55945,"parentid":53465,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Snake Plant\n|Image  = SnakePlant.png\n|HP     = 75-79\n|AscHP  = 78-82\n|Powers = {{BD|Malleable}} 3\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}} {{Power Infobox|Malleable}}\nSnake Plant is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found only in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Snake Plant}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Chomp Chomp\n|Intent = Attack5\n|Effect = Deals (7\u00d73;{{Asc|2|8\u00d73}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Enfeebling Spores\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies 2 {{BD|Frail}} and 2 {{BD|Weak}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Every turn:'''\n* {{Int|Snake Plant|Chomp Chomp}} 65% chance\n* {{Int|Snake Plant|Enfeebling Spores}} 35% chance\n\nCannot use {{Int|Snake Plant|Chomp Chomp}} three times in a row and cannot use {{Int|Snake Plant|Enfeebling Spores}} twice in a row.\n\n<!-- Does this pattern repeat, or return to the randomized moves after? -->\nOn {{Asc|17|Ascension}}, when it uses {{Int|Snake Plant|Enfeebling Spores}} for the first time, its pattern changes to: \n* {{Int|Snake Plant|Chomp Chomp}}\n* {{Int|Snake Plant|Chomp Chomp}}\n* {{Int|Snake Plant|Enfeebling Spores}}\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2608":{"pageid":2608,"ns":0,"title":"Spheric Guardian","revisions":[{"revid":55952,"parentid":53471,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spheric Guardian\n|Image  = SphericGuardian.png\n|HP     = 20\n|Powers = {{BD|Artifact}} 3 <br> {{KW|Block}} 40 <br> {{BD|Barricade}}\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Barricade}}\n'''Spheric Guardian''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that appears in [[Act 2]] and [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Spheric Guardian}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Activate\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = Gains (25;{{Asc|17|35}}) {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Debuff Attack\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|11}}) damage. Applies 5 {{BD|Frail}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Slam\n|Intent = Attack5\n|Effect = Deals (10\u00d72;{{Asc|2|11\u00d72}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Harden\n|Intent = DefendAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|11}}) damage. Gains 15 {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Spheric Guardian''' always starts with {{Int|Spheric Guardian|Activate}}, then uses {{Int|Spheric Guardian|Debuff Attack}}. Afterwards, '''Spheric Guardian''' alternates between using {{Int|Spheric Guardian|Slam}} and {{Int|Spheric Guardian|Harden}} for the rest of the battle.\n\n== In Party With ==\n=== Act 2 ===\nAs an easy pool encounter:\n* Solo\n\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside:\n* 1 {{M|Sentry}}\n\n=== Act 3 ===\nAs a hard pool encounter alongside:\n* 2 random [[Shapes]]\n\n== Tips ==\n* Cards that remove or do damage through {{KW|Block}} are very useful against {{M|Spheric Guardian}}, as it has low HP.\n** {{C|Melter}} is very helpful for removing {{KW|Block}}, and {{C|Judgment}} will instantly kill a {{M|Spheric Guardian}} regardless of its {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{M|Spheric Guardian}} appears in the card art for {{C|Melter}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Weekly Patch 40: Forethought\n** Some minor fixes for Spheric Guardian audio. Removed some code for unused sounds.\n\n* Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!\n** Spheric Guardian's heavy attack is now a multi-hit. 20 -> 10 x 2.\n** Spheric Guardian gets new animations.\n\n* Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance\n** 2 Shapes + Sphere combat, the enemies now attack left -> right.\n\n* Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!\n** Spheric Guardian no longer talks\n** Spheric Guardian nerfed.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"2585":{"pageid":2585,"ns":0,"title":"Spire Shield and Spire Spear","revisions":[{"revid":55954,"parentid":53513,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"== Spire Shield ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spire Shield\n|Image  = SpireShield.png\n|HP     = 110\n|AscHP  = 125\n|Powers = {{BD|Artifact}} 1 ({{Asc|18|2}})\n|Debut  = Act 4\n|Type   = Elite\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Back Attack}}\nSpire Shield is an [[Elite]] enemy found exclusively in [[Act 4]].\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spire Shield}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Bash\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (12;{{Asc|3|14}}) damage. If the Player has an [[Orbs#Orb_Slot|Orb Slot]], there is 50% chance to apply -1 {{BD|Focus}}. Otherwise applies -1 {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Fortify\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = All enemies gain 30 {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Smash\n|Intent = DefendAttack7\n|Effect = Deals (34;{{Asc|3|38}}) damage. (Gains {{KW|Block}} equal to damage dealt.; Gains {{Asc|18|99}} {{KW|Block}}.)}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nEvery three turns, starting from turn 3, it uses {{Int|Spire Shield|Smash}}.\n\nOtherwise has a 50/50 chance of using:\n* {{Int|Spire Shield|Bash}} followed by {{Int|Spire Shield|Fortify}}\n* {{Int|Spire Shield|Fortify}} followed by {{Int|Spire Shield|Bash}}\n\n=== Found With ===\n==== Act 4 ====\n* {{M|Spire Spear}} on the right side of the player.\n\n== Spire Spear ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Spire Spear\n|Image  = SpireSpear.png\n|HP     = 160\n|AscHP  = 180\n|Powers = {{BD|Artifact}} 1 ({{Asc|18|2}})\n|Debut  = Act 4\n|Type   = Elite\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Back Attack}}\nSpire Spear is an [[Elite]] enemy found exclusively in [[Acts#Act 4:The Ending|Act 4]].\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Spire Spear}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Burn Strike\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (5\u00d72;{{Asc|3|6\u00d72}}) damage. (Adds 2 {{C|Burn|Burns}} into your discard pile.; Adds 2 {{C|Burn|Burns}} {{Asc|18|on top of your draw pile}}.)}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Skewer\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (10\u00d73;{{Asc|3|10\u00d74}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Piercer\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = All enemies gain 2 {{BD|Strength}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\nAlways starts with {{Int|Spire Spear|Burn Strike}}.\n\nEvery 3 turns, starting from turn 2, it uses {{Int|Spire Spear|Skewer}}.\n\nOtherwise has a 50/50 chance of using:\n* {{Int|Spire Spear|Burn Strike}} followed by {{Int|Spire Spear|Piercer}}\n* {{Int|Spire Spear|Piercer}} followed by {{Int|Spire Spear|Burn Strike}}\n\n=== Found With ===\n==== Act 4 ====\n* {{M|Spire Shield}} on the left side of the player.\n\n== Notes ==\n* The player begins this elite combat with the [[Debuff]] {{BD|Surrounded}}. This only serves as a telegraph for their {{BD|Back Attack}} mechanic and does not actually add any damage bonus.\n** {{P|Smoke Bomb}} cannot be used while {{BD|Surrounded}}\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Elites]]"}}}]},"2374":{"pageid":2374,"ns":0,"title":"The Guardian","revisions":[{"revid":55809,"parentid":53432,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = The Guardian\n|Image  = TheGuardian.png\n|Icon   = Map-Guardian.png\n|HP     = 240\n|AscHP  = 250\n|Powers = {{BD|Mode Shift}} 30 ({{Asc|9|35}} {{!}} {{Asc|19|40}})\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Boss\n}} {{Power Infobox|Mode Shift}} {{Power Infobox|Sharp Hide}}\n'''The Guardian''' is a [[Boss]] that can appear at the end of [[Act 1]] or the [[Act 3]] event {{E|Mind Bloom}}.\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|The Guardian}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Charging Up\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = Gains 9 {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Fierce Bash\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (32;{{Asc|4|36}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Vent Steam\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Applies 2 {{BD|Weak}} and 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Whirlwind\n|Intent = Attack5\n|Effect = Deals 5\u00d74 damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Defensive Mode\n|Intent = Buff\n|Effect = Gains (3;{{Asc|19|4}}) {{BD|Sharp Hide}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Roll Attack\n|Intent = Attack2\n|Effect = Deals (9;{{Asc|4|10}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Twin Slam\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals 8\u00d72 damage. Loses {{BD|Sharp Hide}}. Gains (30;{{Asc|9|35}} ; {{Asc|19|40}}) {{BD|Mode Shift}}, increased by 10 for each time {{BD|Mode Shift}} triggered this combat.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nRepeats the following pattern:\n#{{Int|The Guardian|Charging Up}}\n#{{Int|The Guardian|Fierce Bash}}\n#{{Int|The Guardian|Vent Steam}}\n#{{Int|The Guardian|Whirlwind}}\n\nWhen Guardian triggers {{BD|Mode Shift}} the current [[Intent]] is replaced with {{Int|The Guardian|Defensive Mode}}.\n\nAfter {{Int|The Guardian|Defensive Mode}}, Guardian uses {{Int|The Guardian|Roll Attack}}, followed by {{Int|The Guardian|Twin Slam}} and {{Int|The Guardian|Whirlwind}}. Then the initial pattern restarts.\n\n<!-- == Hints == \n* Interrupt Fierce Bash by triggering mode shift\n* Play block cards while in Defensive Mode\n* Permanently sources of minus strength good\n-->\n== Trivia ==\n\n* Guardian appears in the artwork of {{C|Spot Weakness}}.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Bosses]]"}}}]},"2553":{"pageid":2553,"ns":0,"title":"Thieves","revisions":[{"revid":55844,"parentid":53442,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"== Looter ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Looter\n|Image  = Looter.png\n|HP     = 44-48\n|AscHP  = 46-50\n|Powers = {{BD|Thievery}} 15 ({{Asc|17|20}})\n|Debut  = Act 1\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Thievery}}\n'''Looter''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that can show up in [[Act 1]] and [[Act 2]].\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Looter}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Mug\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|11}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lunge\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (12;{{Asc|2|14}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Smoke Bomb\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = Gains 6 {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Escape\n|Intent = Escape\n|Effect = Flees combat with your [[Gold]].}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n* Uses {{Int|Looter|Mug}} for the first 2 turns.\n* Has a 50% chance to use {{Int|Looter|Lunge}} or 50% chance to use {{Int|Looter|Smoke Bomb}}.\n** If {{Int|Looter|Lunge}} is used on its third turn, it will then use {{Int|Looter|Smoke Bomb}} next.\n* The turn after {{Int|Looter|Smoke Bomb}} has been used, it will {{Int|Looter|Escape}}.\n\n=== In Party With ===\n\n==== Act 1 ====\nAs a hard pool encounter:\n\n* Solo\n\nAs half of the '''Exodium Thugs''' encounter along with either:\n\n* 1 {{M|Red Louse}}\n* 1 {{M|Green Louse}}\n* 1 {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}\n* 1 {{M|Acid Slime (M)}}\n\n==== Act 2 ====\nAs an easy pool encounter along with:\n\n* {{M|Mugger}}\n\n== Mugger ==\n{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Mugger\n|Image  = Mugger.png\n|HP     = 48-52\n|AscHP  = 50-54\n|Powers = {{BD|Thievery}} 15 ({{Asc|17|20}})\n|Debut  = Act 2\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Thievery}}\n'''Mugger''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that can show up exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n=== Pattern ===\n{{Intents Table/start|Mugger}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Mug\n|Intent = Attack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|11}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Lunge\n|Intent = Attack4\n|Effect = Deals (16;{{Asc|2|18}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Smoke Bomb\n|Intent = Defend\n|Effect = Gains (11;{{Asc|17|17}}) {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Escape\n|Intent = Escape\n|Effect = Flees combat with your [[Gold]].}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Mugger''' has the same pattern as '''Looter'''.\n\n=== In Party With ===\n\n==== Act 2 ====\nAs an easy pool encounter along with:\n\n* {{M|Looter}}\n\n{{Clear}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Looter appears in the Card art for {{C|Flurry of Blows}}.\n* Mugger appears in the Card art for {{C|Clothesline}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Weekly Patch 36: Power Through\n** Slaver/Looter and Slaver/Monster encounters in Act 1 swap positions to prevent Vulnerable + Attack turns.\n\n* Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!\n** Looter is moved from weak monster pool to regular monster pool (only appears after fighting 3 other 'weak' encounters on level 1)\n** Looter + Mugger fight no longer allows you to steal back extra gold if you ran out of gold.\n** Thievery Power now has correct name being applied to the Power.\n\n* Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance\n** Mugger doesn't give back gold it didn't steal\n\n* Day 1 Patch\n** Looter only refunds gold that was stolen now.\n** Thievery power now displays how much gold is stolen per attack.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"1874":{"pageid":1874,"ns":0,"title":"Time Eater","revisions":[{"revid":56425,"parentid":56424,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n| Name   = Time Eater\n| Image  = TimeEater.png\n| Icon   = Map-TimeEater.png\n| HP     = 456\n| AscHP  = 480\n| Powers = {{BD|Time Warp}}\n| Debut  = Act 3\n| Type   = Boss\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Time Warp\n| Image        = Icon TimeWarp.png\n| Description  = Whenever you play a certain number of cards, ends your turn and gains X {{BD|Strength}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToEnemy = Strength\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Draw Reduction\n| Image        = Icon DrawReduction.png\n| Description  = Draw X less cards next turn.\n| Type         = Debuff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = Removed\n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Draw\n}}\n'''Time Eater''' is a [[Boss]] found at the end of [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Time Eater}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Reverberate\n| Intent = Attack5\n| Effect = Deals (7\u00d73;{{Asc|4|8\u00d73}}) damage.\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Head Slam\n| Intent = DebuffAttack6\n| Effect = Deals (26;{{Asc|4|32}}) damage. Applies 1 {{BD|Draw Reduction}}. (;Adds {{Asc|19|2}} {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.)\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw Reduction\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Ripple\n| Intent = DebuffDefend\n| Effect = Gains 20 {{KW|Block}}. Applies 1 {{BD|Vulnerable}}, 1 {{BD|Weak}}(.; and {{Asc|19|1}} {{BD|Frail}}.)\n| GivesToPlayer = Vulnerable, Weak, Frail\n| GivesToEnemy = Block\n}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n| Name   = Haste\n| Intent = Buff\n| Effect = Removes all [[Debuffs]]. Heals to 50% HP. (;Gains {{Asc|19|32}} {{KW|Block}}.)\n| GivesToEnemy = Heal, Block\n}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n'''Time Eater''' will always use {{Int|Time Eater|Haste}} when it is reduced to below half HP. {{Int|Time Eater|Haste}} can only be used once per combat. '''Time Eater''' will use one of the following three attacks each turn:\n* {{Int|Time Eater|Reverberate}} (45% chance)\n* {{Int|Time Eater|Head Slam}} (35% chance)\n* {{Int|Time Eater|Ripple}} (20% chance)\n'''Time Eater''' will not use {{Int|Time Eater|Reverberate}} three times in a row, or {{Int|Time Eater|Head Slam}}/{{Int|Time Eater|Ripple}} twice in a row.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* When playing as the [[Ironclad]], [[Silent]], or [[Defect]], Time Eater will say ''\"Ah... company.\"'' on its first turn.\n** When playing as the [[Watcher]], Time Eater will instead say ''\"Never... Liked... You...\"''.\n\n== Update History ==\n* Weekly Patch 51: Recursion\n** Burn cards no longer trigger Time Eater's ability at end of turn.\n\n* Weekly Patch 42: Reboot\n** Adding a VFX for when your turn ends due to Time Warp power.\n** Updating SFX for Time Warp Power.\n\n* Weekly Patch 40: Forethought\n** Adding SFX for Time Warp, Flight, Constricted, and Entangle Powers.\n\n* Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal\n** Time Eater's Time Warp no longer increments when Curses play themselves.\n\n* Weekly Patch 11: A Library of Features\n** Curses/Statuses that play themselves no longer trigger Powers (Time Warp, After Image, etc)\n\n* Weekly Patch 10: Quality of Life\n** We updated the animations for several monsters! Affected monsters include: Time Eater\n\n* Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!\n** Time Eater now gains less Strength from Time Warp but base damage for attacks increased.\n\n* Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!\n** Time Eater and Champ now show which Powers get removed when they remove them.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Bosses]] [[Category:ToUpdate]]"}}}]},"3055":{"pageid":3055,"ns":0,"title":"Transient","revisions":[{"revid":53501,"parentid":53500,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Transient\n|Image  = Transient.png\n|HP     = 999\n|Powers = {{BD|Fading}} 5 ({{Asc|17|6}}) <br> {{BD|Shifting}}\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}} {{Power Infobox|Fading}} {{Power Infobox|Shifting}}\nThe Transient is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Transient}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Attack\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (20+N; {{Asc|2|30+N}}) damage. N = Current turn, multiplied by 10.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\n\n== Found With ==\n=== Act 3 ===\n* Solo\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]},"3056":{"pageid":3056,"ns":0,"title":"Writhing Mass","revisions":[{"revid":56009,"parentid":55186,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Enemy Infobox\n|Name   = Writhing Mass\n|Image  = WrithingMass.png\n|HP     = 160\n|AscHP  = 175\n|Powers = {{BD|Malleable}} 4 <br> {{BD|Reactive}}\n|Debut  = Act 3\n|Type   = Normal\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Malleable}} \n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Reactive\n|Image        = Icon Reactive.png\n|Description  = Upon receiving attack damage, changes its [[Intent]].\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Does not stack\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Parasite}}\nWrithing Mass is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] found in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Pattern ==\n{{Intents Table/start|Writhing Mass}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Multi Hit\n|Intent = Attack5\n|Effect = Deals (7\u00d73;{{Asc|2|9\u00d73}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Debuff Attack\n|Intent = DebuffAttack3\n|Effect = Deals (10;{{Asc|2|12}}) damage. Applies 2 {{BD|Weak}} and 2 {{BD|Vulnerable}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Big Hit\n|Intent = Attack7\n|Effect = Deals (32;{{Asc|2|38}}) damage.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Block Attack\n|Intent = DefendAttack4\n|Effect = Deals (15;{{Asc|2|16}}) damage. Gains 16 {{KW|Block}}.}}\n{{Intents Table/row\n|Name   = Parasite\n|Intent = DebuffStrong\n|Effect = Permanently adds a {{C|Parasite}} to your deck.}}\n{{Intents Table/end}}\nOn its first turn, it has an (approximately) equal chance to use {{Int|Writhing Mass|Multi Hit}}, {{Int|Writhing Mass|Big Hit}}, or {{Int|Writhing Mass|Debuff Attack}}.\n\n'''Afterwards:'''\n* {{Int|Writhing Mass|Parasite}} 10% chance\n* {{Int|Writhing Mass|Block Attack}} 30% chance\n* {{Int|Writhing Mass|Debuff Attack}} 20% chance\n* {{Int|Writhing Mass|Multi Hit}} 30% chance\n* {{Int|Writhing Mass|Big Hit}} 10% chance\n\n{{Int|Writhing Mass|Parasite}} can only be used once.\n\nThe same move cannot be used (or rerolled via {{BD|Reactive}}) twice in a row.\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"text-align: center; margin:left\"\n|+ Percent Chance based on last used move\n|-\n! Intent\\Used !! Parasite !! Block !! Debuff !! Multi Hit !! Big Hit\n|-\n! Parasite \n\t| - || ~14% || 12.5% || ~14% || ~11%\n|-\n! Block \n| ~33% || - || 37.5% || ~43% || ~33%\n|-\n! Debuff\n| ~22% || ~29% || - || ~29% || ~22% \n|-\n! Multi Hit\n| ~33% || ~43% || 37.5% || - || ~33% \n|-\n! Big Hit\n| ~11% || ~14% || 12.5% || ~14% || -\n|}\n\n== Found With ==\n=== Act 3 ===\n* Solo\n\n== Notes ==\n* Writhing Mass is the only enemy in the game capable of giving the player a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}.\n* {{C|Parasite}} is only added to your deck and not any pile or your hand, so it will only affect future combat encounters.\n\n{{EnemyNav}}\n[[Category:Monsters]]"}}}]}}}}